    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129-a5">

                <pb facs="0197" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg191"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">M. Cologan to the Chinese
                    Plenipotentiaries.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Highness and Excellency</hi>: I received the letter
                    which you were pleased to send me under date the 12th of May, concerning the
                    court ceremony, “and I did not fail to communicate it to my colleagues.</p>
                <pb facs="0198" n="192" xml:id="pg192"/>
                <p>The representatives of the foreign powers, after having considered it, they
                    requested me to inform your highness and your excellency that they can only
                    maintain the demands expressed in my note of the 10th of May.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. J. de Cologan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
